This would have been weaponless too if not for a couple "you begin
bashing monsters with your pick-axe" slips.  (Just goes to show I'm
still not careful enough.)

So after my first ascension, I had originally wanted to give wizards a
shot seeing as they are completely different from valkyries.  Several
wizard deaths on NAO later without much luck, I decided to play some
other classes for a while.  Soon thereafter, NAO started having major
stability problems, and I began playing offline again.  After a few
failed samurai I started playing monks.

Baphomet entered the Dungeons of Doom as a neutral human Monk.  My
starting spellbook was protection (turned out to be pretty useful in
the early game).  A room on Dlvl1 had a lawful altar (quickly
converted) and Dlvl2 held the entrance to the Mines.  I quickly
discovered that, unlike most classes, Monks are built to do the mines
first.  As soon as I was XP:3 I started down.  Most of the levels were
lit, and the Minetown altar was coaligned.  Cleared out the mines
without too much excitement, gaining levels like mad (I think I was XP:
10 on my way back up).  Mine's End was the wine cellar version.  A
gray unicorn had taken residence in Minetown, and I quickly maxed out
my luck throwing gems at him.

On T:6655, in what was only my second or third prayer at an altar, I
was crowned.  I feel like this was probably a negative thing given
that I would have gained the remaining intrinsics in a few levels
anyway, but I never really felt the weight of an increased prayer
timeout.

Dlvl5 and Dlvl6 both had throne rooms (2 for 2 puffs of logic!) and
somewhere around this time I discovered that smoky potions were full
healing (never got a djinni, though).  The entrance to Sokoban was on
Dlvl9; while I was in Soko, an egg hatched into a tame black naga
hatchling, which I promptly forgot about and killed when he got stuck
behind a boulder.  Whoops... Top level was the bag of holding version.

I received Dragonbane and a spellbook of... something as my next
sacrifice gifts, and then continued downward (I had also accumulated
4-5 points of divine protection at this point, and would ultimately
reach naked AC 0).  Dlvl12 was the Big Room, and I nearly YASD'd
myself when what I assumed was a dwarf king turned out to be a master
mind flayer.  I had only started with an INT of 9.  My elven leather
helm saved my life; I resisted a few brain suckings but still got
knocked down to INT 5 and forgot half the dungeon.  I don't remember
killing the MMF... he must have hit a poly trap or something because
once I unihorned my brains back, the next time I went downstairs he
was gone.

Dlvl14 was the quest portal, and also had Demonbane just lying on the
floor.  A third throne room was here as well, which yielded a third
puff of logic.

On T:18868 I realized the lamp I'd been carrying around was magic (it
had gone a few thousand turns with no sign of extinguishing), so I
blessed and rubbed it to score a wish.  I went back and forth between
wishing for the Orb of Fate and a CoMR, but ultimately went with the
cloak.  Thank god.  Within the next 300 turns I ran into *two* giants
who both spawned with wands of death!  I was able to retrieve both of
these with a good number of charges remaining.  Somewhere down here I
ID'ed two of my rings as conflict and free action, respectively.

I found a coaligned altar on Dlvl20 and a coaligned *temple* on
Dlvl21.  Dlvl24 was Medusa and Dlvl25 was the castle.  Drawbridge
smash, yadda yadda yadda.  Castle wand was 0:2.  I wished for 2
blessed ?oCharging (got 1) and blessed fireproof +2 speed boots.
Before charging the wand, I blindfolded myself and offed Medusa.
Perseus' statue had a shield of reflection which I wore for the rest
of the game (removed only to cast spells).

Back on the castle level, I recharged and wished for the blessed Orb
of Fate, an amulet of live saving (I was given strangulation?), an
uncursed fireproof magic marker, and wrested a =oLevitation.  I had a
brain fart and neglected to write genocide scrolls before burning out
my marker writing enchant armor, and decided that I'd genocide stuff
later.  With a source of levitation I was finally free to explore the
rest of the castle, where (naturally) I found another pair of boots of
speed in the armory.

The Valley of the Dead had a blessed +0 helm of brilliance and about 5
XP levels' worth of fresh wraith corpses.  Once I cleared the place
out, I was at AC -19, about 135HP, and in pretty good shape.

Dlvl27 was the first floor of Gehennom and home to Asmodeus.  Paid off
for 6zm.  Dlvl31 was Juiblex, Dlvl32 was Baalzebub (85zm), Dlvl35 was
the entrance to Vlad's (his AoLS was a welcome treasure).  Dlvl36
housed the Wizard of Yendor, Dlvl39 was Orcus (stoned with a
cockatrice corpse for his 0:8 wand).  Got disintegration resistance
from a black dragon corpse.  Around this point I decided to go
genoless.

I found and marked the vibrating square on Dlvl45 (shallow dungeon).
While digging Gehennom out on my way back up, a master lich showed up
and summoned nasties.  One of his summoned demons thought it would be
fun to summon Yeenoghu.  I didn't share his enthusiasm.  Fortunately,
I had a cockatrice corpse in my open inventory (I always pick them up
when they drop because I don't want them wielded against me) and
quickly stoned Yeeno and then the master lich.

On the way back up I killed and ate a wood nymph to gain teleportitis
(had gotten telecontrol at XP:17).  The quest was a breeze; with the
Orb of Fate, Master Kaen's attacks were more than manageable.
Levelported to Dlvl44, climbed the tower, killed a bunch of guys (I
kept a rung of sustain ability in open inventory in case I felt any
waves of psychic energy), zapped Rodney, got the book, levelported to
Dlvl45, performed the invocation, and entered the sanctum.  On T:36455
I got the Amulet of Yendor and began the ascension run.  I ran into
Rodney three more times in the Dungeons and gave him a zap of death
every time.

I used a confused ?oGD on the Plane of Earth, and the Orb of Fate on
the other planes to locate the portals.  Got engulfed twice on Air and
lost about half my HP (~90 from a max of 184).  I arrived on Astral on
T:38091 causing conflict, and saw that Death was left, Famine middle,
and Pestilence right.  I went middle first - lawful.  I went left
second - chaotic (Death sucked about 20 off my max HP before I karate
chopped his ass back to the stone age.  He died a second time to a
zruty :-) ) I clawed my way past Pestilence and the hordes of priests,
angels, liches, and insects to the altar of Chih Sung-Tzu and offered
the Amulet.

Lessons learned this game:

1) Conflict makes many monsters (read: liches) a lot easier to deal
with.  With conflict, liches don't automatically teleport to the
upstair to heal, and you can often land several hits before they
choose to attack you.
2) Don't waste 30000 turns mapping out Gehennom the hard way.  Use
magic mapping if you have it available, or just explore the area from
stair to stair.  The place is tedious enough without having to wander
every last nook and cranny.
3) Cockatrice corpses are the best weapons in the game, hands down.
If you're careful, having one can make your life much much much
simpler.



